# /etc/fstab — larch-os
# Static and identical on every machine: partitions are found by label, so
# nothing here is per-machine. /tmp is left to systemd's stock tmp.mount.
#
# No initramfs: the kernel mounts LARCHSYS (rootfs.squashfs written raw onto the
# partition; a squashfs has no filesystem label, hence PARTLABEL) itself, via
# root=PARTLABEL=LARCHSYS rootfstype=squashfs in the loader entry. Every
# writable path is a mount below, and its mount point ships in the image
# (setup-chroot.sh), since nothing can be created on the read-only root at boot.
#
# LARCHCONF holds all persistent system state and is mounted outside /etc,
# since the /etc overlay would hide a mount inside it. It isn't nofail: without
# it /etc and /var aren't writable and the system can't come up.
#
# /etc is the image's /etc (read-only, lower) under LARCHCONF/etc (upper), so
# tools that replace files by rename (passwd, usermod, timedated, …) work and
# their changes persist. The installer writes this machine's identity into the
# upper layer: hostname, hosts, machine-id and the account files. PID 1 reads
# /etc before the overlay mounts: its units and fstab come from the image, and
# machine-id / hostname come from the kernel command line (systemd.machine_id=,
# systemd.hostname=), matching the upper layer's copies.
#
# /var is overlaid the same way: the image's /var (lower) under LARCHCONF/var
# (upper), so every service's state (NetworkManager, Bluetooth,
# AccountsService, journal, timers, …) persists without per-directory binds,
# while image-owned files nobody has changed (catalogs, caches, the Flathub
# remote) come from whatever image is booted. /var/tmp is tmpfs so unbounded
# temp files can't fill LARCHCONF. LARCHHOME holds the user's home at
# /home/<username>. udisks mounts removable drives under /media/<user>, which it
# must create, hence the tmpfs there.

PARTLABEL=LARCHSYS       /           squashfs  ro                                             0  0
LABEL=LARCHCONF          /conf       ext4      defaults,relatime                              0  2
overlay                  /etc        overlay   lowerdir=/etc,upperdir=/conf/etc,workdir=/conf/etc-work,x-systemd.requires-mounts-for=/conf  0  0
overlay                  /var        overlay   lowerdir=/var,upperdir=/conf/var,workdir=/conf/var-work,x-systemd.requires-mounts-for=/conf  0  0
tmpfs                    /var/tmp    tmpfs     mode=1777,nosuid,nodev,size=25%                0  0
LABEL=LARCHHOME          /home       ext4      defaults,relatime,nofail                       0  2
tmpfs                    /media      tmpfs     mode=0755,nosuid,nodev                         0  0
